## Slash commands available (skills)

| Skill | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **`/x-implement <task>`** | **CANONICAL work command.** 3 phases: Phase 0 (parse + clarify + scope-lock via PROMPT_GENERATOR.md framework with opinionated ambiguity scoring) → Phase 1 (implement, scope-locked) → Phase 2 (self-check + auto-fix critical violations + report). Use this for any non-trivial work. |
| `/x-prompt <task>` | Plan-only alias for `/x-implement --plan-only`. Runs Phase 0 only, outputs the scope contract, stops. Use this when you want a brief to review/share/paste into a ticket without committing to the work. |
| `/x-rules [category]` | List all enforced rules from `.claude/rules.md` |
| `/x-check` | Audit uncommitted/staged changes against the rules (LLM-based, exhaustive sweep) |
| `/x-check-file <path>` | Audit a single file against the rules |
| `/x-add-rule <category> <description>` | Append a new rule to `.claude/rules.md` with auto-numbering |

### `PG` shorthand (Prompt Generator trigger)

Type **`PG <task>`** or **`PG: <task>`** in any message and `/x-implement <task> --plan-only` auto-fires. Default is plan-only — read the brief first, then type "go" to proceed with Phase 1+2. To skip the confirmation step entirely: **`PG <task> --auto`**.

### Decision tree

| You want | Use |
|---|---|
| Plan AND execute the work in one go (with confirmation between phases) | `/x-implement <task>` |
| Plan only — review the brief first, decide later | `/x-prompt <task>` or `PG <task>` |
| Plan AND auto-execute without confirmation | `/x-implement <task> --auto` or `PG <task> --auto` |
| Skip planning entirely (trivial fix) | `/x-implement <task> --skip-prompt` |
| Just audit existing code (no changes) | `/x-check` |

## Layered enforcement

| Layer | Mechanism | Speed | Coverage |
|---|---|---|---|
| L1 | `/x-implement` Phase 2 self-check | Slow (LLM) | Full semantic |
| L2 | `/x-check` (manual sweep) | Slow (LLM) | Full semantic |
| L3 | `.git/hooks/pre-commit` (auto every commit) | Milliseconds | Critical bash patterns |
| L4 | GitHub Actions on PR/push | ~30s | Same critical patterns + PR comments |

L3 + L4 use the same source script: [.claude/scripts/x-precommit.sh](.claude/scripts/x-precommit.sh). Maintained by editing the master + redeploying via [install-hooks.sh](.claude/scripts/install-hooks.sh) and [install-workflows.sh](.claude/scripts/install-workflows.sh).

